# Step 23.6c: a refusal of the pass of the typed notation INSIDE the index of a head is a loud refusal of the frontend. The array type in a typed head (`char[]: v`) waits for the answer of the author
# (diagnostic 34 of the pass, as in a file); the text of the head is read as a document of its own, the pass refuses it, and the frontend reports the message at the statement that holds the head.
include: "<stdlib.h>"
fn: slot_one (@: s char) int
    return: 1
fn: write_array (@: p int) int
    p[slot_one(char[]: v)] := 5
    return: 0
send: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
